  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "10. Shooting Phase",
    "ruleNumber": "10.06",
    "summary": "An [engaged](vsdata:core-rule/engagement-range) unit that has not [Advanced](vsdata:core-rule/advance-move) this turn can shoot this way if it has at least one **[[CLOSE-QUARTERS]](vsdata:weapon-ability/close-quarters)** weapon or is itself a **MONSTER/VEHICLE** unit. Its models are allowed to target enemy units their unit is [engaged](vsdata:core-rule/engagement-range) with. For each attack by a **MONSTER/VEHICLE** model, the Hit roll takes -1 unless the attack uses a **[[CLOSE-QUARTERS]](vsdata:weapon-ability/close-quarters)** weapon against a unit [engaged](vsdata:core-rule/engagement-range) with the firer's unit, and a **[[BLAST]](vsdata:weapon-ability/blast)** weapon still may not target any unit [engaged](vsdata:core-rule/engagement-range) with the firer's unit. Every other model is limited to **[[CLOSE-QUARTERS]](vsdata:weapon-ability/close-quarters)** weapons and to targets [engaged](vsdata:core-rule/engagement-range) with its unit. Attacks follow [Making Attacks](vsdata:core-rule/making-attacks) (04), and for the rest of the phase the unit may not begin an Action.",
